pdfium-oracle — third-party provenance

This directory (`scripts/pdfium-oracle/`) is CI/dev tooling, not shipped library code: it
builds `pdfium_shim`, the external oracle binary `tests/PlumePdf.CorpusTests/PdfiumOracle.cs`
shells out to for SSIM-vs-PDFium parity comparisons. It is never packaged into the PlumePdf
NuGet package. This NOTICE records the provenance of the PDFium call sequences `pdfium_shim.c`
adapts, per the clean-room policy in AGENTS.md's permissive-porting allowance (PDFium is a
named permitted source) — see `pdfium_shim.c`'s own header comment for the fuller narrative;
this file is the standalone attribution record Phase 9 calls out separately.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Base load/render sequence (Phase 8)

The `--self-test`/`--render` load/render call sequence (`FPDF_InitLibrary` ->
`FPDF_LoadDocument`/`FPDF_LoadMemDocument` -> `FPDF_LoadPage` -> `FPDFBitmap_Create` ->
`FPDF_RenderPageBitmap` -> `FPDFBitmap_GetBuffer`) follows bblanchon/pdfium-binaries' own
reference shim, `example/example.c` (MIT-licensed repo wrapper around BSD-3-Clause PDFium
itself — see `licenses/pdfium.txt` in the release archive this shim compiles against).
`pdfium_shim.c` replaces that reference's fixed "input output" PPM dump with the PNG-writing,
argv-driven CLI contract `PdfiumOracle.cs` documents and probes; the PNG encoder itself is an
independent from-scratch implementation of the open PNG/zlib/DEFLATE specifications, not
derived from any PDFium or third-party source.

  Source: bblanchon/pdfium-binaries, `example/example.c`, MIT License (repo wrapper) around
  PDFium (BSD-3-Clause; original code copyright 2014 Foxit Software Inc. / The PDFium
  Authors).
  https://github.com/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries/blob/chromium/8009/example/example.c

