Form-fill call sequence (Phase 9)

The `--render-forms` mode's `FPDF_FORMFILLINFO` callback struct and its
`FPDFDOC_InitFormFillEnvironment` -> `FORM_DoDocumentJSAction` -> `FORM_DoDocumentOpenAction`
-> `FORM_OnAfterLoadPage` -> `FPDF_FFLDraw` -> `FORM_OnBeforeClosePage` ->
`FPDFDOC_ExitFormFillEnvironment` call sequence is written directly against PDFium's own public
header `public/fpdf_formfill.h` (BSD-3-Clause, bundled in the pinned bblanchon/pdfium-binaries
release `install-pdfium-oracle.sh` downloads) — specifically that header's own per-callback
"Interface Version"/"Implementation Required"/parameter doc comments, which name the exact
call order and the minimal required-callback set (`FFI_Invalidate`, `FFI_SetCursor`,
`FFI_SetTimer`, `FFI_KillTimer`, `FFI_GetLocalTime`, `FFI_GetPage`, `FFI_GetRotation`,
`FFI_ExecuteNamedAction` for a non-XFA, non-V8 build) this shim implements as minimal,
non-interactive no-op/stub functions in `pdfium_shim.c`. No PDFium `.cc`/implementation source
was read or copied — only the public, BSD-3-Clause header's own documented public API and its
doc-comment call-sequence guidance, the same "permitted reference" tier `example.c` above
already establishes for this directory. The exact minimal required-callback set and the
widget field dictionary's `/T` (partial field name) requirement — undocumented in the header's
prose, but load-bearing: a standalone top-level widget lacking `/T` is silently never
associated with a `CPDF_FormField` by this exact pinned build, so `FPDF_FFLDraw` has nothing
to synthesize an appearance for — were confirmed empirically against the pinned
`chromium/8009` release before landing, and are recorded in `pdfium_shim.c`'s own
`run_self_test_form_fixture` doc comment.

  Source: PDFium (chromium/pdfium), `public/fpdf_formfill.h`, BSD-3-Clause; original code
  copyright 2014 Foxit Software Inc. / The PDFium Authors.
  https://github.com/chromium/pdfium

